================================================================================
nmail third-party licenses: statically linked system libraries
================================================================================

The following external C/C++ libraries are built from source and linked into
nmail's statically linked binary distributions (HAS_STATIC_EXTLIBS, the
tarballs produced by utils/dist/build-*.sh). A dynamically linked build
resolves them against the host system instead and does not redistribute them,
so this fragment is appended to the combined notices only for static builds.

The macOS build links a few of these (libcurl, expat, iconv, zlib) against the
system libraries under /usr/lib instead; those remain dynamic and are covered
by Apple's own licenses.

This fragment is maintained by hand; keep the versions in sync with those
pinned in utils/dist/Dockerfile.* and utils/dist/build-deps-macos.sh.


